WHAT THE RATIO COLUMN REVEALS:

The ratio (outcome vs wound) tells you whether a category is a hook or a payoff.

High wound, low outcome = strong HOOK, weak payoff. Women describe the problem vividly but don't describe what's different after. Best used for scene/bridge.

Caffeine: 59 wound, 4 outcome. Women talk about living on coffee. Almost none say "I don't need coffee anymore." Strong before-state SCENE — the coffee cup in every frame.
Nap elimination: 22 wound, 1 outcome. Women describe napping extensively. Almost none say "I stopped napping." The wound is vivid, the recovery isn't stated. Reddit is where the nap-outcome language lives, not Amazon.
Mood/anxiety: 54 wound, 9 outcome. Lots of anxiety described, very little "my anxiety went away." Scene language, not angle language.

High outcome, low wound = strong PAYOFF, weak hook. Women describe what changed but don't dwell on what it was like before. Best used for outcome montages and CTA.

Full day: 5 wound, 54 outcome. Almost nobody says "I only had four hours." They say "I have energy all day now." Payoff language, not hook language.
Exercise: 0 wound, 21 outcome. Nobody says "I was too tired to exercise." They say "I'm working out again." Pure payoff.
Identity: 0 wound, 12 outcome. "Feel like myself again" — pure payoff language.
Work productivity: 0 wound, 13 outcome. "Stay focused all day" — pure payoff.

Balanced wound AND outcome = complete angle. Both the scene and the resolution are in the data. These are the strongest testable angles because you have hook AND payoff language.

Brain fog: 34 wound, 28 outcome. Women describe the fog AND describe it lifting. Full angle.
Afternoon crash: 19 wound, 31 outcome. Women describe crashing AND describe getting past it. Manus's finding confirmed — this is the strongest complete angle.
Sleep quality: 14 wound, 18 outcome. Both sides present but less sharp than brain fog or afternoon crash.
Hair/skin: 21 wound, 11 outcome. Both sides present. Visual-proof angle.
Libido: 4 wound, 15 outcome. Mostly outcome language — "libido came back." The wound is understated in Amazon reviews (probably because it's private). Reddit would have the wound side.

